    "final_text": "`buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false` in the query string. The full suite passes (8 tests, 0 failures). With the `src` change stashed, the new test fails.\n\n**Root cause:** `serializeQuery` and `appendQueryValue` in `src/url-builder.js` skipped values with `!value`. That check treats `0` and `false` the same as \"missing\", so both were dropped.\n\n**Fix:** a small helper, `isEmptyQueryValue`, now makes that decision in both places. It skips only `undefined`, `null` and `''`.\n\n- **Empty string:** I kept skipping it, so that behaviour is unchanged. `NaN` is no longer skipped, so it now serializes as `NaN`.\n- **Array items:** the same rule applies inside arrays, so `ids: [0, false, 1]` serializes as `ids=0&ids=false&ids=1`.\n\n**Regression test:** `buildUrl keeps numeric zero and boolean false query values (ISSUE-214)` in `tests/url-builder.test.js`. It covers `retry: 0`, `include_archived: false`, `dry_run: true`, and `null`/`undefined` being skipped. It also covers `0` and `false` inside an array.\n\nI added a `Resolution` section to `ISSUE.md` naming the code path and the test.",
